Track 1: The Timetable Swallows the Hub
- Story & Context: When transit supervisor Sarah Chen deliberately switched Maglev Line 03 into the automated reclamation incinerator to protest halved oxygen rations, the central interchange collapsed into a riot of blaring klaxons and sealed bulkheads. Huddled beneath the carriage of an uncoupled ore car, Mara Vance recorded Chen's frantic radio broadcasts through a magnetic induction coil, matching the frantic chimes of the station's warning glockenspiel to a furiously fingerpicked guitar motif. The resulting track became the clandestine hymn of the lower decks after Vance sang the desperate chorus hook, "Cancel the route, burn the chart on the floor, we only breathe when the train hits the door." Chen’s spanner, discarded on the electrified third rail during her capture, serves as the percussion that opens the song, captured halfway to Proxima Centauri before the sector's power grid was severed forever.
