Track 3: Is That the Final Whistle?
- Story & Context: Decades after the rail mutiny broke the transit spine of the ship, scrap divers in the flooded ballast sector uncovered an unspooled cassette recorder floating inside a frozen maintenance pod. The tape contained a single live take of bowed glockenspiel chimes and nylon guitar recorded by an anonymous woman dying of hypothermia beside a decommissioned steam terminal. Her voice, shivering violently through a cracked respiratory mask, sang the haunting refrain, "Is that the final whistle, or just the hull giving way to the cold?" before the track dissolves into the unyielding groan of vacuum-warped steel girders. Reconstructed by shipboard historians, the recording is now played across generation-ship barracks like a funeral prayer whenever the vessel passes an uncharted celestial body.
